What is the value of $5x + 2y$?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, '41', ARRAY['41'], E'Subtracting the second equation from the first: $(7x + 2y) - (3x + 2y) = 53 - 29$, which gives $4x = 24$, so $x = 6$. Substituting into the second equation: $3(6) + 2y = 29$, so $18 + 2y = 29$, giving $2y = 11$ and $y = 5.5$. Therefore $5x + 2y = 5(6) + 2(5.5) = 30 + 11 = 41$. Alternatively, note that $5x + 2y$ is the average of $(7x + 2y)$ and $(3x + 2y)$: $\\frac{53 + 29}{2} = 41$.', NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 90, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-10-11"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-10-11","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);




